{
  "design_rationale": "Evidence shows positive gain, 2-3 s pure delay (E4 dip for 2.5 s before rise, E8/E3 residual rise 1-2 s), net rates 0.008-0.025/s, drain 0.02-0.032/s at mid-high y, noise <0.02, and strongly nonlinear ss: 0.5->~0.32 (E1), 0.55->~0.40 (E9), 0.57-0.59 rising at 0.55 (E10-E12), 0.6 still rising at 0.65 (E7), 0.8 net +0.023/s at 0.55 (E6). Local DC gain ~1.6 low, >5 near 0.6. Ultimate gain ~1.6, so linear Kp must be <0.8. Chose Kp=0.55, Ki=0.045 (Ti~12.2 s ~ tau), beta=0.9, Tf=0.9 s filter. Feedforward 0.58 at 0.6 from piecewise interpolation of ss points compensates drain so integrator only trims. Far/mid zones give time-optimal coarse fill/drain with braking distance rate*delay~0.06 s to overcome low linear gain without instability, frozen integral prevents windup. Asymmetric slew (up 0.7/s, down 2.0/s) smooths delay-induced overshoot and allows fast shutoff. Absolute safety at 0.82/0.86 protects hard cutoff 0.9 despite unseen true state.",
